WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:05.060
With the exception of Infinity War, Clint
Barton a.k.a. Hawkeye has been a mainstay

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:09.480
of the Avengers gatherings, and the introduction
of his wife Laura in Age of Ultron proved

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.309
that Earth's mightiest heroes could have a
home life as well.

00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:16.390
If the kind, supportive Mrs. Barton looks
familiar, it's probably because you've almost

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:19.439
definitely seen Linda Cardellini in something
before.

00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:22.960
The actress has been active in Hollywood for
more than two decades and has racked up some

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:24.890
impressive credits along the way.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:28.880
From roles in children's favorites of the
late '90s to peak TV appearances, here's where

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.749
you may have seen Cardellini before.

00:00:31.749 --> 00:00:33.390
TGIF

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:38.410
After enjoying a breakout role in ABC's kid-thriller
series Bone Chillers, Cardellini spent a great

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:41.510
deal of her early career in the kid-centric
television circuit.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:46.499
She enjoyed cameo roles in TGIF shows like
Step by Step and Boy Meets World and also

00:00:46.499 --> 00:00:50.579
made appearances on 3rd Rock from the Sun
and the Clueless small screen series.

00:00:50.579 --> 00:00:54.520
Boy Meets World was significant for her because
it was the first role for which she was recognized

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.269
out and about, albeit for all the wrong reasons.

00:00:57.269 --> 00:00:58.550
As she told The A.V.

00:00:58.550 --> 00:00:59.550
Club:

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.629
"I was at my hometown carnival and about eight
kids ran up to me, they couldn't have been

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:05.390
older than 8 years old, and yelled, 'Homewrecker!'"

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:08.310
Hey, those Team Topanga fans can be intense.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.360
Good Burger

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.860
Cardellini's silver screen breakthrough came
by way of Nickelodeon's Good Burger, a bizarre

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.960
fast food film based on a regular sketch from
the TV network's All That.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.360
In the movie, she appears as Heather, a young
woman in a mental institution whose history

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:27.670
may or may not include breaking into a zoo
to "free the kangaroos" at the behest of space

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:28.670
aliens.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:29.670
"I'm a psychopath."

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:30.780
"I'm Ed!"

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:35.390
She'd later reunite with the film's stars,
Kenan Thompson and Kel Mitchell, for an episode

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:38.799
of their buddy comedy, Kenan &amp; Kel.

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:39.799
Strangeland

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:44.710
Shortly after the advent of the AOL chatroom
came Strangeland, a feature-length PSA about

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:46.920
the dangers of meeting strangers online.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:50.810
Although the technology is now outmoded, the
movie's message is still as relevant today

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.979
as it was back then, and Cardellini's turn
as a girl who's abducted after going to the

00:01:54.979 --> 00:01:59.689
fake party of a guy she met on the internet
still produces a lot of terror.

00:01:59.689 --> 00:02:01.429
Freaks and Geeks

00:02:01.429 --> 00:02:05.750
After earning several regular television spots
in series that didn't last, Cardellini landed

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:09.410
the central role of Lindsay Weir in NBC's
Freaks and Geeks.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:13.390
The show featured her as an awkward high schooler
who decides to make friends with some of the

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:18.630
less academically-inclined members of the
student population, much to her parents' disappointment.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:22.470
Although it was cancelled after the first
season, it's since become a cult favorite.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.050
"I love the show.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:27.370
I continue to love it, and I feel so lucky.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:30.780
How can you not be proud of that show?"

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:34.540
It may not have offered her long-term job
security at the time, but the series does

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:40.010
offer her one heck of a highlight reel as
the series continues to draw in new fans.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:41.800
Legally Blonde

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:46.110
Cardellini's appearance in this romantic comedy
taught us all about the unexpected legal importance

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:47.920
of a solid hair care regimen.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:51.910
In Legally Blonde, Cardellini takes the stand
as the daughter of a murdered millionaire

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:55.780
to testify against the client of Reese Witherspoon's
Elle Woods.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:59.111
Cardellini's role might've been small, but
it was hardly superfluous when it comes to

00:02:59.111 --> 00:03:03.010
the overarching plot of Elle Wood's overnight
ascent to master litigator.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:05.920
"You, however, had time to hide the gun, didn't
you, Chutney?

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:06.920
After you shot your father?"

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:07.920
"I didn't MEAN to shoot him!

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.970
I thought it was YOU walking through the door!"

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.500
Scooby Doo

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.820
Although the Scooby-Doo films didn't quite
make her a household name, they did align

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:21.310
her with some very popular teen stars of the
time, including Freddie Prinze, Jr., Sarah

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:23.340
Michelle Gellar, and Matthew Lillard.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.590
And her turn as Velma had some purposefully
provocative moments that are still worth discussing.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:31.840
Thanks to her thick glasses and unusual hair
in the first film, her face wasn't exactly

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:34.720
getting seared into audiences' memories during
the movie.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:38.880
But after her big makeover scene in Scooby
Doo 2: Monsters Unleashed, her true appearance

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.390
became much less of a mystery for moviegoers.

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.250
Brokeback Mountain

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:48.410
Cardellini also had a brief role in Ang Lee's
Brokeback Mountain as Cassie Cartwright, a

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:52.430
small-town waitress who takes a shine to Heath
Ledger's Ennis Del Mar, not knowing he's still

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:55.420
holding a candle for Jake Gyllenhaal's Jack
Twist.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.880
Cardellini admitted that her interest in the
small role first stemmed from her admiration

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.670
for the director and screenwriter.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:01.670
She told The A.V.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:02.670
Club:

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:05.450
"I'm a huge Ang Lee fan and a huge Larry McMurtry
fan.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:07.060
That script is so beautiful.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:11.481
I remember spending 45 minutes auditioning
and thinking, 'I may not get this part, but

00:04:11.481 --> 00:04:15.430
it doesn't matter because I just spent 45
minutes getting directed by Ang Lee.'

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:17.810
When I got the part [...] it was really a
gift and privilege."

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:20.940
ER

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:24.080
Cardellini really got to show off her flare
for the dramatic with her long-standing role

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:29.310
on NBC's ER as Samantha Taggart, a nurse who
is both a recovering alcoholic and a single

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:30.310
mother.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:33.940
She played the character for six seasons,
enduring everything from unstable exes to

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:37.460
a hostage situation at the hospital to an
exploding ambulance.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.990
Although she was able to do other projects
during her five-season run on the show, she's

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:44.900
called the experience of being on the series
a "marathon" and didn't commit to doing any

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:48.960
regular TV work, other than voice roles in
animated series, for the better part of a

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.449
decade afterward.

00:04:51.449 --> 00:04:52.449
Return

00:04:52.449 --> 00:04:56.680
One of Cardellini's post-ER passion projects
was a small film called Return, which featured

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:00.479
her in the lead as a war veteran returning
home to her family and finding that although

00:05:00.479 --> 00:05:04.229
she's wanted nothing more than to be with
them again, she doesn't recognize or feel

00:05:04.229 --> 00:05:05.990
recognized by her old world.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:09.621
The film was one of the first that would feature
Cardellini in every scene, and while it might

00:05:09.621 --> 00:05:13.271
not have been a box office smash, it was one
of several well-reviewed projects that would

00:05:13.271 --> 00:05:16.620
help earn the actress some serious indie cred.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:17.620
Mad Men

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:22.410
Among the many prestige TV shows to take hold
of Hollywood in recent years, AMC's Mad Men

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:26.199
had to have the most buzzy cameo list of all,
Cardellini included.

00:05:26.199 --> 00:05:30.530
In the show's sixth season, she debuted in
her recurring role as Sylvia Rosen, a neighbor

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.189
to Jon Hamm's Don Draper.

00:05:32.189 --> 00:05:35.849
She becomes his part-time lover and, eventually,
full-time obsession.

00:05:35.849 --> 00:05:40.169
Her appearance on the show reveals some staggering
details about his oft-mysterious past.

00:05:40.169 --> 00:05:43.832
For Cardellini, being a part of the awards
season favorite series meant that she'd have

00:05:43.832 --> 00:05:48.310
to keep a set secret, but that extra work
on the home front was worth it because she

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:52.840
earned her first and only Emmy nomination
for her work in the show.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:53.840
Daddy's Home

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:55.999
As genre-bending as her screen career has
been, Cardellini does seem particularly at

00:05:55.999 --> 00:05:57.300
home in the comedy realm.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:01.650
It's what made her a good fit for a guest
role on New Girl and why she was such a scene-stealer

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:05.930
in Grandma's Boy, and Daddy's Home and its
sequel gave the actress another chance to

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:10.490
play around with some other funny people for
a while, namely, Will Ferrell and Mark Wahlberg.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:15.090
In the movies, she stars as Sara, the mother
of two whose new spouse is an ideal step-father

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:19.250
to her children, but whose first husband is
a mess who returns to stir up trouble and

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:21.590
attempt to win back his family from the new
guy.

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:23.240
Antics ensue.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:29.160
"Do over!"

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.880
"That's a do over!"

00:06:30.889 --> 00:06:32.719
Bloodline

00:06:32.719 --> 00:06:36.270
Cardellini's real return to the small screen
scene came by way of Netflix's Bloodline as

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:40.610
Meg Rayburn, the youngest in a tumultuous
family who tries and often fails to broker

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:42.160
peace between her siblings.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:45.979
She starred in the series for three seasons,
which gave her character plenty of room to

00:06:45.979 --> 00:06:49.800
arc into some dark places, and Cardellini
relished the opportunity.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.919
She initially joined the series because of
the talent that she'd get to work with on

00:06:52.919 --> 00:06:56.559
the show but found that working on another
series gave her the opportunity to stretch

00:06:56.559 --> 00:06:59.099
her creative legs in a way films cannot.

00:06:59.099 --> 00:07:00.120
As she told Elle Magazine:

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.620
"I think there are great roles for women in
television because there is time to allow

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:06.219
those characters to evolve."

00:07:06.219 --> 00:07:07.419
Voice work

00:07:07.419 --> 00:07:11.569
In addition to having a diverse portfolio
of screen appearances, Cardellini is also

00:07:11.569 --> 00:07:13.080
a prolific voice actress.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:17.800
She started doing vocal work for video games
before earning a title role in the short-lived

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:20.000
ABC animated series The Goode Family.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:24.240
She'd go on to do voice work for a number
of other cartoon shows, including Scooby-Doo!

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:28.580
Mystery Incorporated, Out There, Regular Show,
and Disney's Gravity Falls.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:31.050
"I'm gonna [to] slipper!"

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:35.259
Her familiar voice may make it difficult for
her to make prank calls, but the ability to

00:07:35.259 --> 00:07:39.370
act off-camera has definitely helped her pay
the bills over the years in between on-screen

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:40.370
gigs!

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:41.370
Thanks for watching!

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:43.560
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.620
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

